  "steps": [
    "Set an oven rack about 6 inches below the broiler and heat the broiler to high.",
    "Stir the sushi vinegar into the warm rice and press it evenly into an 8x8 in baking dish.",
    "Scatter a thin layer of masago over the rice, then 1 tbsp furikake.",
    "Mix the crab, mayo, ponzu, cream cheese and masago in one bowl. Mix the tuna, mayo, gochujang, cream cheese and pepper in another.",
    "Spread the creamy crab over one half of the rice and the spicy tuna over the other half.",
    "Drizzle with mayo and sprinkle with the remaining furikake.",
    "Broil 3-5 minutes, watching closely, until the top is golden and bubbling.",
    "Scoop onto seaweed sheets and eat like hand rolls."
  ],
  "tips": [
    "Credited to Tiffy Cooks. No raw fish, so it is a good sushi bake for a crowd.",
    "Cucumber and avocado slices are good extras in each seaweed scoop."
